From 035c65bc1d023a0d2313cdc3ce066695af6a77de Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 18:38:24 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] spec: ON-DEVICE speculative checkpoints - drafter now BEATS
 plain (8.02 vs 4.5 t/s, byte-clean)

The F-136 correctness fix left DFlash2 correct-but-slow (2.2 t/s): the spec checkpoint
serialized recurrent state through the host at ~1.2 s per draft cycle (measured, new
'spec ckpt cost' counters). LLAMA_SPEC_CKPT_ON_DEVICE=1 routes the six server spec-ckpt
sites through the dormant llama_io_*_device path: save 1.2 s -> 12 ms. Huihui Q4_K +
DFlash2 Q4_K_M, 16-corpus temp0: depth 3 = 8.02 t/s (1.8x plain), depth 7 = 5.54, all
0 degenerate, 12/16 byte-identical to plain (rest fluent tie-flips).
Evidence: research/local-inference/lane-evidence/2026-08-24-ring-repair/.

Rides along, same lane:
- CPU GDN wsize: per-thread scratch offset by CACHE_LINE_SIZE_F32 but allocation was not -
  last thread wrote past the buffer (K>1). Sizing + offset idiom fixed.
- Ring (n_rs_seq) bisect record: CPU k8 KFLIP 16/16 (ring CORRECT on CPU); Vulkan k8 fails
  in every machinery subset that persists bank planes, unaffected by force-sync/fusion-off/
  cont-staging; op-level CPY plane-offset cases (added to test-backend-ops) all PASS -
  mechanism unlocated, diagnostic env gates left in (GGML_VK_FORCE_SYNC,
  LLAMA_RS_BANK_OFF_*, LLAMA_RS_CONV_*, LLAMA_RS_SHIFT_CONT). Ring stays OFF;
  on-device ckpt makes it unnecessary for speed on this class.
